# Placeholder reference only. The application does not automatically load this file.
# Supply notification values privately only for an explicitly enabled CLI/PostgreSQL channel.
WATCHDOG_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=<TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN>
WATCHDOG_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=<TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID>
WATCHDOG_DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=<DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL>
# SQLite CLI database selection uses --database or the explicit monitoring JSON.
# SQLite HTTP (dist/service.js) requires --config, --runtime-root and --database;
# its named environment inputs are PORT and WATCHDOG_READ_API_TOKEN, not database URLs.
# PostgreSQL (dist/postgres-service.js) instead requires WATCHDOG_STORAGE_BACKEND=postgres,
# WATCHDOG_POSTGRES_NAMESPACE, WATCHDOG_POSTGRES_WRITER_URL and WATCHDOG_POSTGRES_READER_URL.
# It also requires PORT, WATCHDOG_READ_API_TOKEN and the distinct WATCHDOG_SCHEDULER_SECRET.
# Supply connection/authentication values privately; see docs/environment-variables.md.
# No RPC, MCP, chain, wallet/private-key or implicit database environment override is supported.
# Non-secret monitoring policy belongs in an explicit monitoring JSON configuration.
